# Isotropy subgroups (crystod-group --supergroup); testsuite section 13
# Validated against ISOSUBGROUP (ISOTROPY Software Suite, https://iso.byu.edu)
# Order-parameter components: arms separated by ";", components within one arm by ","

$ crystod-group --supergroup Pm-3m --irrep GM4- --order-parameter 0 0 a

* Supergroup *
Pm-3m (No. 221)

* Irrep *
GM4-: order parameter dimension 3

* Isotropy subgroup *
GM4-(0,0,a) -> P4mm (No. 99)
cell size 1, index 6
sublattice basis (parent primitive units): (1,0,0), (0,1,0), (0,0,1)
conventional basis (parent conventional units): (0,0,1), (1,0,0), (0,1,0)
origin: (0,0,0)

Conventions and validation: ISOSUBGROUP (https://iso.byu.edu):
H. T. Stokes, S. van Orden and B. J. Campbell, "Tool for Generating
Isotropy Subgroups of Crystallographic Space Groups",
J. Appl. Cryst. 49, 1849-1853 (2016).

